# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this file, what lands in a commit depends on each contributor's `core.autocrlf`, so a
# Windows checkout can silently rewrite every line of a file it barely touched. That happened on
# the architecture-hardening line: ~60 files were rewritten CRLF -> LF, inflating the diff roughly
# sixfold (9075/3920 raw vs 5416/261 real) and burying the actual changes for review and blame.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes the choice explicit and identical for everyone: git normalizes text
# files to LF on commit and checks them out as LF on every platform. Rust, Node, and the shells in
# use here all read LF fine on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one interpreter here that genuinely needs CRLF. PowerShell reads LF fine, so
# .ps1 stays on the LF default rather than churning every script in scripts/ for no benefit.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
